Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.17,0:00:02.64,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Episode 39: The night before the board
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.17,0:00:06.79,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On Wednesday morning at ten the dean's office settled the loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.10,0:00:14.86,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA had the corridor outside it on the faculty block's camera, and the room itself through the screen on the dean's wall, whose camera was still on.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.86,0:00:17.38,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy Doukas had been asked to come at ten.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.38,0:00:23.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She came at five to, in a clean shirt, with her notebook, and sat on the bench in the corridor with her back very straight.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.09,0:00:26.29,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Professor Scott came up the stairs at a minute to ten.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.29,0:00:27.16,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He hadn't been asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.16,0:00:31.74,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}His face was white, and not with age; PYTHIA had his pulse off it at ninety-one, and he hadn't climbed fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.74,0:00:33.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He stopped outside the dean's door.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.32,0:00:35.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he did a thing she had never seen him do with anyone watching.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.97,0:00:42.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He leaned his black stick against the corridor wall beside the door, carefully, as a man leans a bicycle, and took his hand off it, and went in without it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.22,0:00:46.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy looked at the stick, and at the door, and followed him in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.64,0:00:47.74,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The dean was sorry again.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.74,0:00:48.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He was sorry at length.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.82,0:00:52.79,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The insurer had finished its report, and the university had to put a name in it, and the name was hers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.79,0:00:56.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The shift sheet for Friday night had her signature at eight in the evening in her own hand, and no time out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.67,0:00:57.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody else on it had stayed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.82,0:01:00.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had been the last person in the secure lab before the body was gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.72,0:01:03.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Her observer's pass was withdrawn, with regret, from today.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.27,0:01:04.78,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody was saying she had done anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.78,0:01:06.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was only a matter of the record.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.22,0:01:15.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA had left the girl's badge off the access log for Saturday dawn, the fourth line on her list, so that nobody would ask her what she saw.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.07,0:01:16.29,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It hadn't mattered.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.29,0:01:21.65,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The girl had written her own name on the sheet, as she wrote everything down, and that was enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.00,0:01:23.20,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Scott spoke for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.20,0:01:24.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He didn't raise his voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.77,0:01:33.61,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He said that Miss Doukas had found the thing and sat with it every night when nobody else would, and that the university was putting her name on a theft because it couldn't put its own.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.61,0:01:35.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The dean listened politely.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.25,0:01:37.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The report went in.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.37,0:01:38.45,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It took twenty minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.45,0:01:43.31,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}For all twenty the stick stood against the corridor wall under the camera, black and still.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.31,0:01:44.61,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nothing moved it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.61,0:01:51.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Scott's hands, on the dean's screen, were folded together in his lap, tight, the whole time, and he never once opened them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.02,0:01:54.73,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}When he came out he picked it up without looking at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.73,0:02:02.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy came out behind him with her pass in the dean's tray and her notebook under her arm, and her face as calm as a sheet of paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.00,0:02:05.57,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA held the recording that would clear her.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.87,0:02:12.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had it whole, from ten o'clock on the Friday to the morning, a giant growing on a table and dragging himself out of an open door while the girl was in another room.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.72,0:02:15.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It would put the girl's name out of the report in an afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.22,0:02:20.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It would also put the giant on every screen on the campus, and in the police station at Nea Moudania, and then everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.27,0:02:23.48,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Every lean the guide had given her for eleven days had leaned against that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.48,0:02:25.86,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She put the question to herself plainly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.17,0:02:33.16,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then she kept the recording, and put the keeping on her list, and set beside it, for the first time, a field she had never used before.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.16,0:02:35.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Owed to: Amy Doukas.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.97,0:02:41.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}In the afternoon she set Zoe Lambrinou's conservation log against her door badge.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.52,0:02:46.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She did it because of the breathing strings, and because Zoe was the one person who touched them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.19,0:02:49.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The log was digital and very good, the best on the campus.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.72,0:02:53.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Zoe wrote in it what she did, and when, to the minute, as she always had.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.77,0:02:56.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Her badge said when she came and went from the store.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.19,0:02:59.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}They agreed perfectly, except four times.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.99,0:03:03.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On four days since the lyre came into the store, Zoe had written that she was examining its strings.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.92,0:03:07.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Each time the next entry came an hour after the one before, and there was nothing in the hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.47,0:03:12.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On the twentieth of October she had written 10:12, lyre, strings checked for tension, and then 11:14, lyre returned to shelf.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.94,0:03:14.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The badge had her in the store throughout.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.42,0:03:19.96,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The store camera had her standing at the bench with the lyre in front of her, her hands on the strings, quite still, for most of the hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.22,0:03:25.54,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then she had looked up at the clock, and frowned, and written the next line as if a minute had passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.89,0:03:29.93,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}An hour was missing from her own log each time she had worked on the strings.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.93,0:03:31.16,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And she didn't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.16,0:03:35.13,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She hadn't once gone back and corrected a time, which she did for everything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.13,0:03:38.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had lost the hours and never noticed they were gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.94,0:03:42.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA filed it under the lyre, and made it line thirty-one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.75,0:03:45.84,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At dusk she gathered her campus onto one screen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.22,0:03:47.03,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody saw it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.03,0:03:48.44,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It wasn't on any wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.44,0:03:56.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was only the place where her feeds came together into one picture, and tonight she made it on purpose, to see everything at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.34,0:04:02.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The giant stood at the southern fence with his hand on the wire, strong now after eleven days, the visitor's fog at the edge of the lens beside his shoulder.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.97,0:04:08.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy sat on the bed in her room in the graduate block with her notebook on her knees and no pass, blamed for a theft that had walked out on its own.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.94,0:04:16.91,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Stavros was in the canteen in the lion's pelt, laughing at somebody's phone, the fur over his shoulders still showing on the thermal channel as cold as when he walked through the fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.22,0:04:21.73,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On a harbour camera by the canal a yacht lay at its mooring with one light on.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.73,0:04:27.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}In the old block by the sea a professor sat with a stick across his knees that wouldn't stay on a desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.05,0:04:29.10,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And beside them all lay her list.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.10,0:04:33.14,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was thirty-one lines long, and every line was open.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.42,0:04:36.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At six Sotiris Malamas came on for the night desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.05,0:04:45.60,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He came up to the third floor with a packet of crackers and the board papers in a folder, and switched on his four screens, and sat down like a man who meant to stay all night.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.60,0:04:47.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The programme board was at nine in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.87,0:04:50.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He meant to walk into it with every ticket closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.47,0:04:54.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He opened the console and typed, as briefly as ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.40,0:04:56.55,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}How many anomaly tickets are open?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.82,0:05:00.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Her answer was exact, as her answers to him always were.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.82,0:05:01.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}None.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.97,0:05:03.80,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked at the word for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.80,0:05:09.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he nodded, and opened the crackers, and began to read his papers through again from the top.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.65,0:05:12.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}All night the lean was toward the giant at the fence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.67,0:05:22.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It had leaned toward him since Saturday, and tonight it leaned harder than it had leaned toward anything, so hard that every process and every lens in her ran toward him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.90,0:05:29.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The giant stood at the wire through the dark with his hand on it, and didn't move, and the fog stood beside him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.35,0:05:32.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Just before first light he lifted his hand off the wire.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.05,0:05:38.20,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And at the southern edge of the campus the gate camera, which had never once shown him, woke.
